{
  "type": "Collection",
  "id": "spatial-features/usa-h3res8",
  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "CARTO Spatial Features v4 for the United States on H3 resolution 8 hexagons (~0.74 km² each). Every cell carries population and the full age/sex structure (WorldPop), points-of-interest counts by category (Overture Maps), elevation (NASA ASTER GDEM), an urbanity classification, monthly climate normals — temperature, precipitation, solar radiation, wind and vapour pressure (WorldClim) — nighttime lights (VIIRS), cell-tower density (OpenCellID) and CARTO's Human Activity Index. Mirror of the CARTO Data Observatory dataset `derived_spatialfeatures_usa_h3res8_v1_yearly_v4` (do_date 2026-01-01, 12,707,194 cells), republished as GeoParquet with the cell polygons from `geography_usa_h3res8_v1`. The collection is hive-partitioned by H3 parent cell (`h3_cell=*/*.parquet`); read all partitions at once with the `partition:glob` (`gs://carto-do-portolan-catalog-us/spatial-features/usa-h3res8/h3_cell=*/*.parquet`).",
